Taking the supremum over $t\in[0,1]$ gives
\begin{align*}
 \sup_{0\le t\le1}
 \left|\int_0^{t/\varepsilon}g(Y(s))\,ds\right|
 &\le\int_0^1|g(Y(s))|\,ds
 +
 \max_{0\le m\le N}
 \left|\int_1^{1+m}g(Y(s))\,ds\right| 
 +\max_{0\le k<N}A_k.
\end{align*}
Multiplying by $\sqrt\varepsilon$ and using Minkowski's inequality,
\eqref{cell_l2}, \eqref{ns_end}, and \eqref{12_bdd}, we obtain
\begin{align*}
 \left\|\sup_{0\le t\le1}|F_\varepsilon^g(t)|\right\|_2
 &\le
 \bigl(\sqrt\varepsilon+C_{d,K}\sqrt{\varepsilon N}\bigr)\|g\|_2
 \le C_{d,K}\|g\|_2,
\end{align*}
since $\varepsilon N\le1$ and $\varepsilon\le1$.
Hence,  \eqref{ns_intbd} follows immediately
and 
the assertion for differences follows by linearity.
